the phrase "4." The rules obey the principle of compositional semantics—the semantics of a phrase is a function of the semantics of the subphrases. Figure 23.9 shows the parse tree for $3+ ( 4 \div2 )$ according to this grammar. The root of the parse tree is Exp(5), an expression whose semantic interpretation is 5.

